<b>Episode 11: "Fireworks of Love"</b>

02:18.340 --> 02:20.990
<b>Episode 11: "Fireworks of Love"</b>

02:18.370 --> 02:20.990
<b>Episode 11: "Fireworks of Love"</b>

02:20.990 --> 02:24.330
There've been fewer and fewer 
people coming to swim, too.

02:25.240 --> 02:28.500
Business management is exhausting.

02:28.800 --> 02:33.400
I can't just shut down Grandma's 
business, though. I have to—

02:34.130 --> 02:35.270
Yeah?

02:36.320 --> 02:38.490
You're working late.

02:38.490 --> 02:41.140
I made coffee. Want some?

02:41.140 --> 02:43.320
Yeah, thanks.

02:43.320 --> 02:45.890
You're the one who told Riho 
not to overwork herself.

02:45.890 --> 02:48.520
Guess you weren't in any position to talk.

02:48.520 --> 02:51.400
I'm the one running this business, remember?

02:51.400 --> 02:53.520
There's a lot I have to do.

02:53.960 --> 02:58.280
Though I'm sure it'll get a bit easier 
once the beach hut wraps up.

02:58.730 --> 02:59.820
I guess.

03:00.300 --> 03:02.620
It's sad to think of it ending, though.

03:03.130 --> 03:05.850
The beach hut was fun in its own way.

03:07.760 --> 03:09.160
Wow...

03:09.660 --> 03:12.170
You've got some challenging books here.

03:12.540 --> 03:14.390
Typical Tokyo U student.

03:14.940 --> 03:17.250
I only used them to study 
for the entrance exams.

03:17.250 --> 03:20.510
I usually only need to read 
something once for it to...

03:23.270 --> 03:24.550
stick in my memory.

03:24.550 --> 03:27.110
Yeah? You're pretty smart, then.

03:27.520 --> 03:29.400
I guess you know everything, huh?

03:30.160 --> 03:32.000
About studying, sure.

03:32.000 --> 03:34.870
Outside of that, there are 
plenty of things I don't know.

03:33.100 --> 03:35.810
<b>The Complete Works of Natsume Soseki</b>

03:38.190 --> 03:39.960
Like a girl's heart?

03:43.490 --> 03:47.120
Yep. That's the kind of thing 
I understand the least.

03:47.860 --> 03:49.660
All lies.

03:49.660 --> 03:52.040
You're very perceptive.

03:52.040 --> 03:55.260
I bet you've already realized how 
a certain someone really feels.

03:56.420 --> 03:58.170
Which someone?

03:58.170 --> 04:02.170
Sounds like you have at least 
a vague idea of who I mean.

04:03.280 --> 04:05.270
I don't. That's why I'm asking.

04:09.760 --> 04:11.040
You want to know?

04:12.830 --> 04:15.580
Then... shall I tell you?

04:16.640 --> 04:19.570
I really have no interest 
in that kind of thing.

04:20.230 --> 04:21.570
What, now?

04:21.570 --> 04:25.110
Are you saying you're more into 
<i>this</i> kind of thing?

04:27.370 --> 04:30.840
Stop it! I don't like when you guys 
joke around about that!

04:30.840 --> 04:32.200
Oh, really?

04:32.200 --> 04:35.500
Then can I ask you one more thing?

04:35.500 --> 04:37.210
Wh-What?

04:37.740 --> 04:39.540
You know, Hayato...

04:41.040 --> 04:43.930
The stars look beautiful tonight.

04:43.930 --> 04:46.100
Do you think it'll be clear tomorrow?

04:50.390 --> 04:52.890
<b>The Complete Works of Natsume Soseki</b>

04:56.910 --> 04:58.090
Who knows?

04:58.090 --> 05:01.530
I don't have time to think 
about that stuff right now.

05:02.000 --> 05:06.670
I already made up my mind to revive 
my grandma's business within a year.

05:06.670 --> 05:10.790
So until I can be sure that 
I'll be able to pull it off,

05:11.260 --> 05:15.830
sorry to say it, but I don't have time to 
think about stars or weather forecasts.

05:19.940 --> 05:21.660
That said...

05:23.410 --> 05:26.840
The coffee you make really is good.

05:27.240 --> 05:32.460
I do hope I'll be able to take my time 
enjoying it while watching the stars someday.

05:37.390 --> 05:39.280
What are you talking about?

05:39.280 --> 05:40.150
Huh?

05:40.150 --> 05:44.680
I was literally just talking about 
the stars and the weather.

05:44.680 --> 05:46.150
Wha?!

05:46.880 --> 05:48.330
Well, whatever.

05:48.330 --> 05:51.160
The stuff smart people say 
never makes sense, anyway.

05:51.680 --> 05:52.780
I'm going to bed.

05:52.780 --> 05:55.450
Y-Yeah... Goodnight.

05:57.320 --> 05:59.170
Oh, right.

05:59.450 --> 06:02.820
You know, the moon is beautiful tonight, too.

06:06.040 --> 06:08.180
You totally knew what I was talking about!

06:08.510 --> 06:09.640
Goodnight.

06:10.680 --> 06:11.940
Hey!

06:13.810 --> 06:14.930
This is exhausting.

06:17.430 --> 06:22.260
I guess that means his response 
to my confession is on hold for now.

06:29.840 --> 06:31.770
You've gotta be kidding me!

06:31.770 --> 06:34.330
How the heck does a bathtub break?!

06:34.330 --> 06:37.550
Well, what do you expect 
from a house that old?

06:37.550 --> 06:41.580
Yeah, but it's gonna be a blast 
going to a bathhouse together!

06:41.580 --> 06:45.090
Someone should be over to fix it tomorrow.

06:45.090 --> 06:48.590
If we're fixing it anyway, 
let's just upgrade it to the latest style.

06:48.590 --> 06:50.750
You know, with jets and stuff.

06:50.750 --> 06:52.390
We can't afford that.

06:53.350 --> 06:56.910
At least get us a new toilet, then!

06:56.910 --> 06:59.180
Don't make me repeat myself.

06:59.620 --> 07:03.580
Get us a new toilet! 
Get us a new toilet! Get us a new toilet!

07:02.480 --> 07:04.220
Look...

07:04.220 --> 07:08.250
I mean, the bidet attachment is like 
the kind they have at old inns!

07:08.250 --> 07:09.470
It scares me!

07:09.470 --> 07:10.990
So come on!

07:10.990 --> 07:13.990
All right, fine. I'll think about it.

07:13.990 --> 07:15.360
Really?!

07:16.410 --> 07:21.000
Come to think of it, we did visit 
the bathhouse with Grandma, didn't we?

07:21.000 --> 07:25.750
Oh, yeah, it was around this time last year 
when the boiler broke, wasn't it?

07:25.750 --> 07:27.500
Yeah, I remember!

07:27.500 --> 07:30.760
Wow, it's really been that long, huh?

07:31.400 --> 07:36.560
Grandma told us to have some coffee milk, 
even though we didn't have money...

07:36.560 --> 07:40.080
Cut it out! You're gonna make me cry, too!

07:40.080 --> 07:41.270
Ami-chan.

07:41.560 --> 07:44.190
You can't take your duck into the bath.

07:44.190 --> 07:46.270
Why not?! It's cute!

07:46.270 --> 07:50.650
<b>Ami</b>

07:46.520 --> 07:48.990
Everyone loves a rubber duckie!

07:48.990 --> 07:50.650
And you need to tie up your hair.

07:54.500 --> 07:56.390
There's no one here!

07:57.120 --> 08:01.910
Hurry up, you guys! The place is all ours!

08:02.320 --> 08:03.770
Ouka-san!

08:05.200 --> 08:07.000
Tsuruga-Style Ninja Arts:

08:07.000 --> 08:08.670
Soap Bar Shuriken!

08:09.020 --> 08:09.920
Wai—

08:14.580 --> 08:18.490
How naïve! You thought a trick 
like that would work on m—

08:18.930 --> 08:20.930
Here we go!

08:24.580 --> 08:28.190
Come on! I told you, 
no horsing around in the bath!

08:28.190 --> 08:31.180
Ouka-chan was the one 
horsing around that time.

08:31.180 --> 08:32.440
Yep.

08:32.440 --> 08:36.350
Never a dull moment with you girls, eh?

08:36.350 --> 08:39.580
It's proper manners 
to use the bathhouse quietly.

08:41.090 --> 08:43.070
The wagashi shop lady!

08:43.070 --> 08:46.400
Your abs are as fabulous as ever, I see!

08:46.400 --> 08:47.580
Stop that!

08:47.580 --> 08:50.340
W-Well, let's get in.

08:50.340 --> 08:52.120
Hey, Riho...

08:53.170 --> 08:54.220
What's up?

08:57.970 --> 09:00.390
Sorry. Never mind.

09:03.230 --> 09:04.200
Ow!

09:04.200 --> 09:07.350
Aw, c'mon, don't be a wimp.

09:07.350 --> 09:10.610
It's gotta be this hot, 
or it ain't a real bath.

09:10.610 --> 09:13.990
No, even for a real bath, that's too hot!

09:13.990 --> 09:16.490
Quit your bellyaching! C'mon!

09:17.340 --> 09:19.520
Sounds noisy over there, too.

09:19.520 --> 09:21.740
Ami-chan, no swimming in the bath!

09:21.740 --> 09:26.590
Wow! For a skinny thing, you've sure 
got a big one, youngster!

09:26.590 --> 09:28.170
Shut up!

09:30.130 --> 09:33.380
Hey, what's Hayacchi got that's so big?

09:33.380 --> 09:35.450
H-How should I know?!

09:36.630 --> 09:40.260
Honestly, goofing around 
like that at his age...

09:40.620 --> 09:44.010
Anyway, how's it been for you girls,

09:44.010 --> 09:46.270
living together with Hayato-kun?

09:46.270 --> 09:47.450
"How's it been"?

09:47.450 --> 09:48.770
What do you mean?

09:48.770 --> 09:51.520
I mean, don't you find yourself 
starting to like him?

09:51.520 --> 09:55.460
He's a good kid on the inside, 
and the outside isn't half bad, either.

09:57.400 --> 10:00.410
O-Of course we haven't!

10:00.410 --> 10:02.860
He's so insensitive and tactless—

10:02.860 --> 10:05.040
Sure, I like Hayacchi!

10:05.040 --> 10:09.670
He bought me takoyaki and 
a kebab sandwich the other day!

10:09.670 --> 10:12.090
Oh, really? Good for you.

10:12.090 --> 10:14.840
Come to my place for some daifuku next time.

10:14.840 --> 10:16.760
I love you!

10:17.620 --> 10:21.760
Th-The heat's making me dizzy, 
so I'm getting out now.

10:21.760 --> 10:25.520
Now, hold on. I haven't heard from you yet.

10:25.950 --> 10:28.090
The last time we talked about this,

10:28.090 --> 10:31.020
we told you we hadn't even thought about it.

10:31.020 --> 10:33.240
But who knows if that's 
still the case, right?

10:33.240 --> 10:35.900
Hey, lady! I wanna eat some mitarashi dango!

10:35.900 --> 10:37.650
And something salty, too!

10:38.180 --> 10:39.690
What about you, Riho?

10:42.080 --> 10:44.860
How do you feel about Hayato?

10:44.860 --> 10:45.780
Huh?

10:47.460 --> 10:48.910
How do I feel?

10:48.910 --> 10:52.510
Well, I think he's 
working hard to run the café,

10:52.510 --> 10:56.870
but I wish he didn't act 
so unfriendly toward customers.

10:57.450 --> 10:59.700
That's not what I'm talking about.

11:02.160 --> 11:04.680
I'm getting dizzy, too.

11:07.880 --> 11:13.190
<i>This isn't the time to be talking 
about whether we like him or not.</i>

11:13.530 --> 11:17.720
<i>We need to get Familia, 
Grandma's business, back on its feet.</i>

11:18.620 --> 11:22.200
<i>I'm sure that's how Hayato feels, too.</i>

11:28.710 --> 11:30.730
<i>So I...</i>

11:30.730 --> 11:31.710
Riho.

11:33.680 --> 11:36.840
I like Hayato.

11:37.770 --> 11:38.710
Huh?

11:39.330 --> 11:41.640
As a man, of course.

11:41.640 --> 11:43.220
You do too, don't you?

11:44.440 --> 11:46.970
L-Like I said, I don't...

11:46.970 --> 11:53.370
even look... at Hayato-kun... that... way.

11:55.510 --> 11:58.320
I see. So you don't mind, then?

11:58.700 --> 12:00.490
Huh? Mind what?

12:03.250 --> 12:07.700
I told Hayato that I like him.

12:11.780 --> 12:14.000
Buy us coffee milk!

12:14.000 --> 12:17.840
Buy us coffee milk! Buy us coffee milk!

12:17.000 --> 12:20.220
Buy it yourself. You just got paid.

12:17.840 --> 12:20.220
Coffee milk! Coffee milk!

12:20.220 --> 12:21.510
You miser!

12:22.930 --> 12:25.720
I'll make caffè latte for you 
when we get back.

12:25.720 --> 12:26.760
Really?!

12:27.260 --> 12:29.080
Want some too, Hayato?

12:29.080 --> 12:30.770
Let's have it together!

12:30.770 --> 12:34.270
I don't like sweet stuff. 
Just make me the usual.

12:34.270 --> 12:35.560
Got it.

12:38.980 --> 12:40.540
We're back!

12:40.540 --> 12:42.320
Took you long enough.

12:42.320 --> 12:44.490
Girls need more time than boys!

12:44.840 --> 12:48.000
Oh, I forgot I'm in charge 
of breakfast tomorrow.

12:48.000 --> 12:49.870
I'll be home after I buy some stuff.

12:49.870 --> 12:52.410
Oh, okay. Thanks.

12:52.410 --> 12:53.370
Ow!

12:53.370 --> 12:55.620
Ow, ow, ow...

12:53.890 --> 12:57.290
You're gonna send a girl out 
shopping on her own at this hour?

12:57.290 --> 12:58.860
Quit kicking me over everything!

12:58.860 --> 13:01.710
Uh... I'll be fine by myself.

13:02.960 --> 13:03.840
Let's go.

13:04.660 --> 13:08.600
If anything happens to anyone 
on my staff, it's my responsibility.

13:08.910 --> 13:11.850
I'll go with you. 
Let's get this done and go home.

13:11.850 --> 13:13.230
S-Sure...

13:13.230 --> 13:16.890
Hey, want me to cook for a change?

13:16.890 --> 13:19.400
You don't need to do a thing, Ami-chan.

13:19.400 --> 13:21.390
Aw, why not?

13:21.390 --> 13:23.240
Come on, let's go home.

13:25.690 --> 13:26.990
You know...

13:27.360 --> 13:32.490
You didn't have to buy so much just because 
stuff's cheaper at the end of the day.

13:32.490 --> 13:36.250
What are we gonna do with all these 
shiitake mushrooms and bean sprouts?

13:38.770 --> 13:43.140
I told Hayato that I like him.

13:45.240 --> 13:46.500
Hello? Riho?

13:47.510 --> 13:48.990
Uh, what?

13:48.990 --> 13:52.010
What's going on? 
You've been out of it since we left.

13:52.010 --> 13:54.840
N-Nothing's going on!

13:54.840 --> 13:57.020
M-Maybe I'm just dehydrated.

13:57.020 --> 13:59.340
I did stay in the bath too long.

14:02.800 --> 14:03.900
Hayato-kun?

14:05.530 --> 14:06.900
<b>Cold</b>

14:05.530 --> 14:06.900
<b>Cold</b>

14:05.530 --> 14:06.900
<b>Cold</b>

14:12.240 --> 14:14.040
Here. Don't tell Ami.

14:15.920 --> 14:17.000
Take it.

14:17.000 --> 14:18.900
Th-Thanks...

14:20.050 --> 14:21.260
<i>Why?</i>

14:22.020 --> 14:24.680
<i>Why are you being so nice to me?</i>

14:25.660 --> 14:29.180
<i>Are you giddy because Akane 
told you she liked you?</i>

14:29.640 --> 14:32.440
<i>Did that make you happy?</i>

14:35.780 --> 14:36.810
Well, how's it going?

14:37.180 --> 14:38.780
How's what going?

14:39.490 --> 14:40.810
I-I mean...

14:40.810 --> 14:42.940
Familia's business. Y'know.

14:42.940 --> 14:45.820
Oh. Decent enough, I guess.

14:45.820 --> 14:48.330
The beach hut did stay in the black,

14:48.330 --> 14:50.700
but not by as much as I expected.

14:51.360 --> 14:54.740
<i>What answer did you give her?</i>

14:55.220 --> 14:57.560
Is that gonna be enough?

14:57.560 --> 15:00.500
Dunno. All we can do is do our best.

15:00.880 --> 15:03.690
It worries me to hear 
the owner talking like that.

15:03.690 --> 15:05.000
Well, stop worrying.

15:05.440 --> 15:09.010
I've been thinking about 
new menu items and events for fall.

15:06.420 --> 15:10.040
<i>So how do you feel about me, then?</i>

15:10.580 --> 15:13.890
<i>Am I just staff? Or a housemate?</i>

15:14.770 --> 15:16.790
That's good, I guess.

15:18.400 --> 15:20.020
<i>I don't want that.</i>

15:20.930 --> 15:23.190
<i>I'm the oldest of all of us.</i>

15:23.190 --> 15:27.960
<i>That's why I've always worked 
my hardest for Familia, and for Grandma.</i>

15:28.410 --> 15:32.110
<i>But the truth is, how I feel about
 Hayato-kun... I'm also in...</i>

15:34.560 --> 15:35.620
What're you doing?

15:36.130 --> 15:39.310
We're gonna make the others worry. 
Let's go in.

15:39.310 --> 15:41.000
S-Sure.

15:42.070 --> 15:44.120
<i>It's just the two of us right now.</i>

15:45.350 --> 15:46.500
Hey...

15:47.460 --> 15:50.280
<i>If I'm gonna tell him, now's the time!</i>

15:54.240 --> 15:56.440
C'mon, let's go.

16:00.270 --> 16:01.440
So tired...

16:07.670 --> 16:08.840
I...

16:10.390 --> 16:14.390
I think I'm in love with you, Hayato-kun.

16:15.570 --> 16:16.530
Huh?

16:20.710 --> 16:23.540
What would you do if I told you 
that out of the blue?

16:24.230 --> 16:26.580
I guess it'd be a problem for you, huh?

16:27.390 --> 16:29.300
What am I even talking about?

16:31.600 --> 16:34.050
Nah, it wouldn't be a problem.

16:34.400 --> 16:36.280
It'd make me happy, like anyone would be.

16:36.280 --> 16:37.180
Huh?

16:37.670 --> 16:40.560
But even if it were true,

16:40.560 --> 16:43.310
there's still no telling 
how the café will hold up,

16:43.610 --> 16:46.140
so I don't have time to think 
about that kinda thing.

16:46.900 --> 16:47.810
That's fine!

16:48.090 --> 16:48.760
Huh?

16:48.760 --> 16:50.870
It if makes you happy, that's enough!

16:50.870 --> 16:51.820
What?

16:52.760 --> 16:53.990
Goodnight!

16:54.430 --> 16:55.570
Wait... Riho?

16:57.280 --> 17:00.950
I seriously don't know what the right 
answer is in these situations...

17:03.880 --> 17:05.930
Yum!

17:08.130 --> 17:10.090
Thank you for coming by!

17:11.120 --> 17:13.590
It's finally slowing down a...

17:14.720 --> 17:16.940
No, not like that.

17:17.340 --> 17:20.240
It's fine. I can do it myself.

17:20.240 --> 17:23.480
You don't have to be shy. I'll show you how.

17:23.480 --> 17:26.230
You don't know how to work 
with these beans, do you?

17:26.230 --> 17:29.480
Come on. Watch closely.

17:29.880 --> 17:32.230
Hey! Something's touching me!

17:32.800 --> 17:34.360
Yep. I know.

17:34.360 --> 17:35.740
You...

17:39.540 --> 17:41.950
What are you two doing?!

17:41.950 --> 17:44.330
This is not a hostess bar!

17:46.070 --> 17:48.900
What?! I'm not doing anything!

17:56.930 --> 18:00.360
Uh, I'm gonna go buy some paper filters.

18:03.970 --> 18:06.030
Touching isn't allowed.

18:06.030 --> 18:07.020
Huh?!

18:08.340 --> 18:09.650
At a hostess bar.

18:10.550 --> 18:14.400
What's your game, hanging all over 
Hayato-kun right in front of me?!

18:14.750 --> 18:18.530
What's the problem? 
There aren't any customers here.

18:18.530 --> 18:22.410
Besides, you don't have 
feelings for him at all, right?

18:23.280 --> 18:26.160
That's right. I don't.

18:27.010 --> 18:28.670
Is that what you expected me to say?!

18:29.120 --> 18:31.790
Of course I like Hayato-kun, too!

18:31.790 --> 18:35.130
So it pisses me off when you do 
stuff like that in front of me!

18:36.820 --> 18:40.170
<i>Being a ladies' man is exhausting.</i>

18:40.170 --> 18:43.070
Man, I couldn't believe 
what was going on at that café.

18:43.070 --> 18:47.140
I know, right? The waitresses 
were really at each other's throats.

18:47.140 --> 18:50.430
"Of course I like him, too!" Was that it?

18:50.430 --> 18:52.460
I dunno who they were talking about,

18:52.460 --> 18:54.920
but I guess there's 
a real ladies' man out there.

18:59.200 --> 19:00.780
It's time to stop this!

19:01.180 --> 19:03.530
I thought it seemed noisy in here!

19:03.900 --> 19:08.160
What are you arguing about?! 
Tell me right now!

19:09.960 --> 19:11.920
Damn it! This is my fault!

19:11.920 --> 19:15.040
They're fighting because 
I'm too damn attractive!

19:16.040 --> 19:17.800
Um...

19:17.800 --> 19:19.010
What are these?

19:19.010 --> 19:22.030
Super-shiny mud balls that I made!

19:22.030 --> 19:23.800
You play by dropping them.

19:23.800 --> 19:25.960
If your ball breaks, you lose!

19:25.960 --> 19:29.720
No matter who wins, you have to 
agree to stop fighting! Got it?

19:30.600 --> 19:32.220
Ami-chan...

19:33.760 --> 19:35.060
Sorry, Riho.

19:35.940 --> 19:38.860
You just wouldn't come out and say it,

19:38.860 --> 19:41.320
so I thought I'd rile you up a little.

19:41.710 --> 19:43.570
Why did you have to do that?

19:43.570 --> 19:47.040
Because every time 
there's something you want to say,

19:47.040 --> 19:48.950
you hold back and bottle it up.

19:49.230 --> 19:54.570
It felt a little unfair for me to be the only 
one doing things my own way.

19:54.570 --> 19:56.210
It was making me feel bad.

19:57.040 --> 20:00.220
Sorry I upset you.

20:01.090 --> 20:06.220
I-It's fine. I guess I got too angry, too.

20:06.680 --> 20:10.730
But now we can finally talk to 
each other from the same perspective.

20:11.180 --> 20:13.720
Even among family, a battle is a battle.

20:13.720 --> 20:14.980
And I won't lose.

20:15.310 --> 20:17.430
Well, neither will I!

20:20.770 --> 20:21.990
You guys!

20:23.300 --> 20:26.490
Stop fighting over me!

20:27.200 --> 20:30.250
I told you I have no intention of 
getting into that stuff right now!

20:30.520 --> 20:32.600
Hayato-kun...

20:32.600 --> 20:34.800
We weren't fighting. Right?

20:34.800 --> 20:35.500
Right.

20:36.090 --> 20:39.180
Actually, when you talk to us like that...

20:39.820 --> 20:41.630
It kind of pisses me off.

20:41.630 --> 20:43.420
Er... Uh...

20:43.420 --> 20:45.390
Don't worry, Hayacchi!

20:45.770 --> 20:49.180
This is just a dropping contest.

20:49.180 --> 20:51.890
No matter who wins, it's just a game.

20:51.890 --> 20:53.430
Dropping...

20:54.230 --> 20:55.400
A game?

20:55.750 --> 20:59.280
You know, the moon is beautiful tonight, too.

20:59.280 --> 21:02.650
I think I'm in love with you, Hayato-kun.

21:02.650 --> 21:05.550
<i>Being a ladies' man is exhausting.</i>

21:05.550 --> 21:08.070
<i>...ladies' man... 
ladies' man... ladies' man...</i>

21:10.260 --> 21:12.890
You're all messing with me!

21:12.890 --> 21:15.540
I think he got the wrong idea.

21:16.130 --> 21:17.330
It's fine.

21:17.630 --> 21:20.500
He'll understand how serious 
we are soon enough.

21:21.440 --> 21:24.470
I won't hold back anymore.

21:24.870 --> 21:26.890
I don't intend to, either.

23:03.890 --> 23:06.150
Bathroom...

23:20.340 --> 23:21.770
<i>Shiragiku?</i>

23:22.830 --> 23:25.580
<i>What is she doing in Grandma's room?</i>

23:27.000 --> 23:41.940
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

23:27.000 --> 23:41.940
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

23:27.490 --> 23:30.300
Let's guess what the last episode 
will be! Battle Tournament!

23:30.300 --> 23:31.480
Battle against who?!

23:31.480 --> 23:32.930
Hayato-kun gets arrested.

23:32.400 --> 23:32.930
Hey!

23:32.930 --> 23:34.510
Hayato-kun and I get together.

23:33.680 --> 23:34.510
Hey!

23:34.510 --> 23:36.010
Hayato-kun becomes my boyfriend.

23:36.010 --> 23:37.470
I'm not falling for that again!

23:37.470 --> 23:40.160
Meow, meow, meow! 
I make a baby with Hayato-kun!

23:40.160 --> 23:41.580
Keep your clothes on!
